cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tessera or refer to its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "Tessera: a programming language designed by measurement against language models"
abstract: >-
  Tessera is a programming language for software that language models write and
  people review. Its design decisions are made by measurement rather than taste:
  a harness has models solve programming tasks from a single language reference,
  compiles every answer, and records pass rate, attempts and token cost per
  variant of the language. The repository holds the specification, two compilers
  (a frozen reference in Rust and a self-hosting one written in Tessera), the
  runtime, the standard modules, the measurement harness and the examples,
  including a DOOM-style engine used as a proof point.
type: software
authors:
